{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "01936",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 0.64,
      "end_seconds": 8.3,
      "duration_seconds": 7.66,
      "text": "doctor, your next patient is here. I've done the basics, I'll read them out in a moment"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 8.8,
      "end_seconds": 12.65,
      "duration_seconds": 3.85,
      "text": "Thanks, that's helpful. Hello, please sit. What's been happening?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 14.59,
      "end_seconds": 21.16,
      "duration_seconds": 6.57,
      "text": "doctor, I'll sit in if that's okay, I know what's been happening"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 23.26,
      "end_seconds": 27.2,
      "duration_seconds": 3.94,
      "text": "I'm here because of drinking most nights."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 28.11,
      "end_seconds": 36.87,
      "duration_seconds": 8.76,
      "text": "Doctor, I've got the readings for you. Temperature 36.9, oxygen saturation is 97 percent. BP is 121 over 82, pulse 78."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 37.99,
      "end_seconds": 38.99,
      "duration_seconds": 1.0,
      "text": "okay, noted"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 57.6,
      "end_seconds": 58.88,
      "duration_seconds": 1.28,
      "text": "Since when exactly?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 60.08,
      "end_seconds": 62.33,
      "duration_seconds": 2.25,
      "text": "I've had it since Friday."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 63.08,
      "end_seconds": 65.83,
      "duration_seconds": 2.75,
      "text": "Is it bearing on you a lot?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 67.47,
      "end_seconds": 74.59,
      "duration_seconds": 7.12,
      "text": "Well, uh, it's... hard to say, it's kind of... I don't know—"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 75.15,
      "end_seconds": 80.83,
      "duration_seconds": 5.68,
      "text": "Take your time. Mild, moderate, or severe, if you had to pick?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 81.46,
      "end_seconds": 86.55,
      "duration_seconds": 5.09,
      "text": "Maybe a four out of ten on a bad day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 87.45,
      "end_seconds": 94.89,
      "duration_seconds": 7.44,
      "text": "and the other thing I wanted to mention is that I can't really—"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 94.99,
      "end_seconds": 103.79,
      "duration_seconds": 8.8,
      "text": "Sorry, what was I saying, tell the doctor about the other thing, that's what worries me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 105.88,
      "end_seconds": 108.73,
      "duration_seconds": 2.85,
      "text": "I, I was getting to that!"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 109.73,
      "end_seconds": 114.38,
      "duration_seconds": 4.65,
      "text": "That's fine, one at a time. I'll ask about everything."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 116.27,
      "end_seconds": 125.07,
      "duration_seconds": 8.8,
      "text": "Oh, and an upset stomach in the mornings. That's been about the same, about a month."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 128.36,
      "end_seconds": 136.97,
      "duration_seconds": 8.61,
      "text": "Tell me a bit more about it: how bad it gets, how often, and whether anything makes it better or worse."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 138.08,
      "end_seconds": 153.11,
      "duration_seconds": 15.03,
      "text": "so, honestly, once or twice a day i'd say moderate i'd rather know what's going on than keep guessing well, I've had poor sleep too, for about two weeks"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 154.05,
      "end_seconds": 160.49,
      "duration_seconds": 6.44,
      "text": "alright, have you had drinking most nights before, or is this the first time?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 161.56,
      "end_seconds": 167.68,
      "duration_seconds": 6.12,
      "text": "I had a similar thing last winter. It It went away."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 169.75,
      "end_seconds": 176.24,
      "duration_seconds": 6.49,
      "text": "let me check a few things any confusion, yellow eyes or black stools?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 178.3,
      "end_seconds": 191.42,
      "duration_seconds": 13.12,
      "text": "No, uh, no confusion, no yellow eyes, no black stools. I did have shaky hands at one point, but that went away on its own."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 192.46,
      "end_seconds": 195.13,
      "duration_seconds": 2.67,
      "text": "have you had any vomiting blood?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 196.17,
      "end_seconds": 200.24,
      "duration_seconds": 4.07,
      "text": "Not that I've noticed, no vomiting blood."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 201.19,
      "end_seconds": 203.22,
      "duration_seconds": 2.03,
      "text": "is your chest okay generally?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 204.51,
      "end_seconds": 206.38,
      "duration_seconds": 1.87,
      "text": "No problems with breathing."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 208.07,
      "end_seconds": 211.62,
      "duration_seconds": 3.55,
      "text": "Any health conditions I should have on record?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 213.56,
      "end_seconds": 215.53,
      "duration_seconds": 1.97,
      "text": "I've got heart disease."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 216.81,
      "end_seconds": 218.28,
      "duration_seconds": 1.47,
      "text": "Is that everything?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 218.95,
      "end_seconds": 226.4,
      "duration_seconds": 7.45,
      "text": "Sorry, you know, what was I saying, I've had thin bones for two years now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 227.66,
      "end_seconds": 229.11,
      "duration_seconds": 1.45,
      "text": "Is that everything?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 231.13,
      "end_seconds": 236.06,
      "duration_seconds": 4.93,
      "text": "I have diabetes. I've had an irregular heartbeat, yes"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 237.3,
      "end_seconds": 238.66,
      "duration_seconds": 1.36,
      "text": "Is that everything?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 253.83,
      "end_seconds": 256.81,
      "duration_seconds": 2.98,
      "text": "Are there any illnesses in your family?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 258.7,
      "end_seconds": 260.51,
      "duration_seconds": 1.81,
      "text": "My son has asthma."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 261.5,
      "end_seconds": 264.04,
      "duration_seconds": 2.54,
      "text": "Now some background about your lifestyle."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 266.02,
      "end_seconds": 279.93,
      "duration_seconds": 13.91,
      "text": "I only drink at family occasions. I quit smoking around ten years ago. Lots of rice, lentils and some fruit. I hardly move around during the day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 280.93,
      "end_seconds": 283.69,
      "duration_seconds": 2.76,
      "text": "have you got any known allergies?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 284.72,
      "end_seconds": 294.69,
      "duration_seconds": 9.97,
      "text": "Actually, I think I reacted to some antibiotic once, years ago. I don't remember which one, or what happened exactly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 297.61,
      "end_seconds": 301.39,
      "duration_seconds": 3.78,
      "text": "What do you take on a normal day?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 302.99,
      "end_seconds": 310.56,
      "duration_seconds": 7.57,
      "text": "It's a... um, I can't remember what it's called. It's a small white one."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 312.61,
      "end_seconds": 315.33,
      "duration_seconds": 2.72,
      "text": "Do you remember what it's for?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 316.9,
      "end_seconds": 327.67,
      "duration_seconds": 10.77,
      "text": "For the stent, I believe. My husband sets them out for me, I just take what I'm given. Alendronate, once a week."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 332.97,
      "end_seconds": 335.1,
      "duration_seconds": 2.13,
      "text": "Do you know the dose?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 336.89,
      "end_seconds": 348.33,
      "duration_seconds": 11.44,
      "text": "it's 70 milligrams i take sitagliptin, 100 milligrams, once a day. Warfarin, 3 milligrams, in the evening for the blood thinning"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 349.35,
      "end_seconds": 360.46,
      "duration_seconds": 11.11,
      "text": "doctor, um, I think the last prescription for the warfarin was 6 milligrams we changed it at the last visit"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 361.21,
      "end_seconds": 366.04,
      "duration_seconds": 4.83,
      "text": "right do you happen to have the current prescription here?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 367.7,
      "end_seconds": 371.57,
      "duration_seconds": 3.87,
      "text": "I don't think I have it with me"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 373.26,
      "end_seconds": 377.35,
      "duration_seconds": 4.09,
      "text": "Let me look at the area, I'll be gentle."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 379.27,
      "end_seconds": 381.66,
      "duration_seconds": 2.39,
      "text": "Hold that for a second."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0052",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 392.12,
      "end_seconds": 398.91,
      "duration_seconds": 6.79,
      "text": "your liver edge is felt slightly below the ribs and there is a fine tremor"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0053",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 402.75,
      "end_seconds": 423.42,
      "duration_seconds": 20.67,
      "text": "thank you, you can get dressed right, here's what I'm thinking the most likely explanation is harmful alcohol use with liver strain. Fatty liver is still possible so, to recap quickly you've had drinking most nights, since Friday, and no yellow eyes or confusion"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0054",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 425.31,
      "end_seconds": 427.96,
      "duration_seconds": 2.65,
      "text": "mm, you know, that's right"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0055",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 429.3,
      "end_seconds": 459.97,
      "duration_seconds": 30.67,
      "text": "I'm sending you for liver blood tests because of alcohol use. I'd like to arrange a blood count for alcohol use. I'm going to put you on thiamine, 100 milligrams, three times a day, long term. You take it by mouth. It's for alcohol-related nutritional deficiency. I'll put all of this in writing so you don't have to remember it. Cut down gradually and do not stop suddenly on your own if you drink heavily"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0056",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 462.02,
      "end_seconds": 480.82,
      "duration_seconds": 18.8,
      "text": "Don't skip meals, and try to eat smaller portions more often through the day. The alcohol support service would be the right next step, I'll refer you. And please bring the latest prescription or the medicine boxes to the next visit, so we can settle the dose."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0057",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 481.79,
      "end_seconds": 489.21,
      "duration_seconds": 7.42,
      "text": "I understand. Could I get an ultrasound of the liver done? A friend had it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0058",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 490.11,
      "end_seconds": 499.62,
      "duration_seconds": 9.51,
      "text": "I wouldn't order it today if anything changes, we'll reconsider i'd like you back after the tests that's all from me any questions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0059",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 500.87,
      "end_seconds": 502.47,
      "duration_seconds": 1.6,
      "text": "That's clear, thanks."
    }
  ]
}